PART 6 — Additional engineering requirements
These requirements apply across all 16 phases. They are important because a project this large can easily become difficult to maintain.
6.1 Agent execution must be stateful
Never rely on an LLM conversation alone to remember an entire task.

Every execution should have a persistent record:
Execution
 ├── Execution ID
 ├── Agent ID
 ├── User objective
 ├── Current plan
 ├── Current task
 ├── Completed tasks
 ├── Pending tasks
 ├── Tool calls
 ├── Tool results
 ├── Errors
 ├── Checkpoints
 ├── Permissions
 └── Final report


If the application crashes, the agent should reconstruct its execution state from persistent storage.
6.2 Use an event-driven architecture
Every important operation should produce an event.

Examples:
agent.started
agent.planning
task.created
task.started
task.completed
tool.discovered
tool.called
tool.failed
mcp.connected
mcp.disconnected
computer.action_started
computer.action_verified
memory.created
conversation.followup_detected
agent.completed


The backend should publish these events to the frontend through WebSockets.

This makes live task monitoring possible.
6.3 Build a proper permission system
Create permission categories:
Permission	Example
Read	Read a document
Write	Create a document
Modify	Edit an existing file
Delete	Delete a file
Execute	Run a command
Install	Install software
Network	Access external websites
Credentials	Use stored credentials
Financial	Make a purchase or payment
Administrative	Perform privileged system operations

Allow users to define which agents can perform which operations.

Support session-based approvals and narrowly scoped authorization rather than asking for permission on every harmless operation.
6.4 Build an observability system
The application should make it possible to investigate what happened.

Record:
- Agent decisions and selected actions.
- Tool calls and results.
- Execution duration.
- Errors.
- Retries.
- Model usage.
- Token consumption.
- MCP connection events.
- Permission decisions.
Do not expose private internal reasoning traces. Display useful plans, action summaries and execution results instead.
6.5 Do not build every component from scratch
Reuse mature libraries where appropriate.
Functionality	Suggested implementation
Desktop interface	Tauri
Frontend	React
Backend	FastAPI
Local inference	llama.cpp
Browser automation	Playwright
GUI image processing	OpenCV
OCR	Tesseract
Linux accessibility	AT-SPI2
Linux desktop integration	D-Bus / GIO
Windows application automation	UI Automation / COM
Database	PostgreSQL
Vector search	pgvector
Task scheduling	APScheduler or a dedicated worker
MCP	Official MCP SDKs
Testing	pytest and frontend testing tools

These are implementation choices, not mandatory dependencies for every component.

